#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "reftable.blockSize"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:7
msgid ""
"The size in bytes used by the reftable backend when writing blocks.  The "
"block size is determined by the writer, and does not have to be a power of "
"2. The block size must be larger than the longest reference name or log "
"entry used in the repository, as references cannot span blocks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:12
msgid ""
"Powers of two that are friendly to the virtual memory system or filesystem "
"(such as 4kB or 8kB) are recommended. Larger sizes (64kB) can yield better "
"compression, with a possible increased cost incurred by readers during "
"access."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:15
msgid ""
"The largest block size is `16777215` bytes (15.99 MiB). The default value is "
"`4096` bytes (4kB). A value of `0` will use the default value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "reftable.restartInterval"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:21
msgid ""
"The interval at which to create restart points. The reftable backend "
"determines the restart points at file creation. Every 16 may be more "
"suitable for smaller block sizes (4k or 8k), every 64 for larger block sizes "
"(64k)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:24
msgid ""
"More frequent restart points reduces prefix compression and increases space "
"consumed by the restart table, both of which increase file size."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:28
msgid ""
"Less frequent restart points makes prefix compression more effective, "
"decreasing overall file size, with increased penalties for readers walking "
"through more records after the binary search step."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:30
msgid "A maximum of `65535` restart points per block is supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:33
msgid ""
"The default value is to create restart points every 16 records. A value of "
"`0` will use the default value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "reftable.indexObjects"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:37
msgid ""
"Whether the reftable backend shall write object blocks. Object blocks are a "
"reverse mapping of object ID to the references pointing to them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:39
msgid "The default value is `true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "reftable.geometricFactor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:45
msgid ""
"Whenever the reftable backend appends a new table to the stack, it performs "
"auto compaction to ensure that there is only a handful of tables. The "
"backend does this by ensuring that tables form a geometric sequence "
"regarding the respective sizes of each table."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:49
msgid ""
"By default, the geometric sequence uses a factor of 2, meaning that for any "
"table, the next-biggest table must at least be twice as big. A maximum "
"factor of 256 is supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "reftable.lockTimeout"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/reftable.txt:56
msgid ""
"Whenever the reftable backend appends a new table to the stack, it has to "
"lock the central \"tables.list\" file before updating it. This config "
"controls how long the process will wait to acquire the lock in case another "
"process has already acquired it. Value 0 means not to retry at all; -1 means "
"to try indefinitely. Default is 100 (i.e., retry for 100ms)."
msgstr ""
